{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-14-1","title":"Jeremiah 14:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The grievous famine, 7 causes Jeremiah to pray. 10 The Lord will not be intreated for the people. 13 Lying prophets are no excuse for them. 17 Jeremiah is moved to complain for them.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3399. B.C. 605. The word.This discourse is supposed to have been delivered after the fourth year of Jehoiakim. The Hebrew {batzaroth,} rendered dearth, signifies restraint, that is, \"when the heaven is shut up that there is no rain;\" which Houbigant thinks happened early in the reign of Zedekiah.</p>\n<p>the dearth. Heb. the words of the dearths, or restraints. 17:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-2","title":"Jeremiah 14:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>mourneth. 4:28; 12:4; Isa 3:26; Ho 4:3; Joe 1:10 the gates. Isa 24:4,7; 33:9 they. 8:21; La 2:9; 4:8,9; 5:10; Joe 2:6 the cry. 11:11; 18:22; Ex 2:24; 1Sa 5:12; 9:16; Job 34:28; Isa 5:7; 15:5 Zec 7:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-3","title":"Jeremiah 14:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>their nobles. 1Ki 18:5,6 pits. 2:13; 1Ki 17:7; 2Ki 18:31; Joe 1:20; Am 4:8 they were. 2:26,27; 20:11; Ps 40:14; 109:29; Isa 45:16,17 covered. 4; 2Sa 15:30; 19:4; Es 6:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-4","title":"Jeremiah 14:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the ground. Le 26:19,20; De 28:23,24; 29:23; Joe 1:19,20 the plowmen. Joe 1:11,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-5","title":"Jeremiah 14:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Job 39:1-4; Ps 29:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-6","title":"Jeremiah 14:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>the wild. 2:24; Job 39:5,6 they.They sucked in the air, for want of water, to cool their internal heat.</p>\n<p>their. 1Sa 14:29; La 4:17; 5:17; Joe 1:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-7","title":"Jeremiah 14:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>though. Isa 59:12; Ho 5:5; 7:10 do. 20,21; De 32:27; Jos 7:9; Ps 25:11; 115:1; Eze 20:9,14,22 Da 9:9,18,19; Eph 1:6,12 for our. 2:19; 3:6; 5:6; Ezr 9:6,7,15; Ne 9:33,34; Da 9:5-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-8","title":"Jeremiah 14:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>the hope. 17:13; 50:7; Joe 3:16; Ac 28:20; 1Ti 1:1 saviour. Isa 43:3,11; 45:15,21 in time. Ps 9:9; 37:39,40; 46:1; 50:15; 91:15; 138:7; 2Co 1:4,5 why. Ps 10:1 a wayfaring. Jud 19:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-9","title":"Jeremiah 14:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>cannot. Nu 11:23; 14:15,16; Ps 44:23-26; Isa 50:1,2; 51:9; 59:1 art. Ex 29:45,46; Le 26:11,12; De 23:14; Ps 46:5; Isa 12:6; Zec 2:5 2Co 6:16; Re 21:3 we are called by thy name. Heb. thy name is called upon us. 15:16; Isa 63:19; Da 9:18,19; *margins leave. 1Sa 12:22; Ps 27:9; Heb 13:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-10","title":"Jeremiah 14:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>have they. 2:23-25,36; 3:1,2; 8:5; Ho 11:7,9 refrained. 2:25; Ps 119:101 the Lord. 6:20; Am 5:22; Mal 1:8-13 he will. 31:34; 44:21,22; 1Sa 15:2; 1Ki 17:18; Ps 109:14,15; Ho 8:13; 9:9 Heb 8:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-11","title":"Jeremiah 14:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>7:16; 11:14; 15:1; Ex 32:32-34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-12","title":"Jeremiah 14:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>they fast. 11:11; Pr 1:28; 28:9; Isa 1:15; 58:3; Eze 8:18; Mic 3:4; Zec 7:13 and when. 6:20; 7:21,22; Pr 15:8; 21:27; Isa 1:11-15 but. 9:16; 15:2,3; 16:4; 21:7-9; 24:10; 29:17,18; Eze 5:12-17; 14:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-13","title":"Jeremiah 14:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Ah. 1:6; 4:10 behold. 5:31; 6:14; 8:11; 23:17; 28:2-5; Eze 13:10-16,22; Mic 3:11; 2Pe 2:1 assured peace. Heb. peace of truth.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-14","title":"Jeremiah 14:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>The prophets. 23:25,26; 27:10,14; 28:13; 29:21; 37:19; Isa 9:15; Zec 13:3; 1Ti 4:2 I sent. 23:14-16,21-32; 27:15; 28:15; 29:8,9,31; Isa 30:10,11; 2Th 2:9-11 divination. 27:9,10; 29:8,9,31; Eze 12:24; 13:6,7,23; 21:29; Mic 3:11; Zec 10:2 and the. 23:26; Isa 30:10; La 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-15","title":"Jeremiah 14:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Sword and famine shall not. 5:12,13; 6:15; 8:12; 20:6; 23:14,15; 28:15-17; 29:20,21; 31,32 1Ki 22:25; Eze 14:10; Am 7:17; 2Pe 2:1-3,14-17; Re 19:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-16","title":"Jeremiah 14:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the people. 5:31; Isa 9:16; Mt 15:14 be cast. 7:33; 9:22; 15:2,3; 16:4; 18:21; 19:6,7; Ps 79:2,3 for. 2:17-19; 4:18; 13:22-25; Pr 1:31; Re 16:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-17","title":"Jeremiah 14:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>let mine. 8:18,21; 9:1; 13:17; Ps 80:4,5; 119:136; La 1:16; 2:18; 3:48,49 for. Isa 37:22; La 1:15; 2:13; Am 5:2 with a very. 30:14,15; Ps 39:10; Mic 6:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-18","title":"Jeremiah 14:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>go forth. 52:6,7; La 1:20; 4:9; Eze 7:15 yea. 6:13; 8:10; 23:21; De 28:36,64; Isa 28:7; La 4:13-16 go about, etc. or, make merchandise against a land, and menacknowledge it not. 2:8; 5:31; Mic 3:11; 2Pe 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-19","title":"Jeremiah 14:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>utterly. 6:30; 15:1; 2Ki 17:19,20; Ps 78:59; 80:12,13; 89:38; La 5:22 Ro 11:1-6 hath. 12:8; Zec 11:8,9 no healing. 8:22; 15:18; 2Ch 36:16; La 2:13 we. 8:15; Job 30:26; La 4:17; 1Th 5:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-20","title":"Jeremiah 14:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>We acknowledge. 3:13,25; Le 26:40-42; Ezr 9:6,7; Ne 9:2; Ps 32:5; 51:3; 106:6-48 Da 9:5-8; 1Jo 1:7-9 for. 2Sa 12:13; 24:10; Job 33:27; Ps 51:4; Lu 15:18-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-21","title":"Jeremiah 14:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>not abhor. 19; Le 26:11; De 32:19; Ps 51:11; 106:40; La 2:7; Am 6:8 for. 7; Ps 79:9,10; Eze 36:22,23; 39:25; Da 9:7,15-19; Eph 2:7 disgrace. 3:17; 17:12; Ps 74:3-7,20; 106:45; La 1:10; 2:6,7,20; Eze 7:20-22 Eze 24:21; 43:7; Da 8:11-13; Lu 21:24; Re 11:2 remember. Ex 32:13; Le 26:42-45; Ps 74:2,18-20; 89:39,40; 106:45 Isa 64:9-12; Zec 11:10,11; Lu 1:72; Heb 8:6-13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-14-22","title":"Jeremiah 14:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Are. 10:15; 16:19; De 32:21; Isa 41:29; 44:12-20 vanities. De 32:21; 1Ki 17:1; 18:1; Ps 74:1,2; Zec 10:1,2; Ac 14:15-17 Art. 5:24; 10:13; 51:16; De 28:12; 1Ki 8:36; 17:14; 18:39-45; Job 5:10 Job 38:26-28; Ps 147:8; Isa 30:23; Joe 2:23; Am 4:7; Mt 5:45 wait. Ps 25:3,21; 27:14; 130:5; 135:7; Isa 30:18,23; La 3:25,26; Mic 7:7 Hab 3:17-19</p>"}]}